<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Corn down, soybeans mostly steady.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Corn down, soybeans mostly steady.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>FOB Gulf corn values were down mostly two cents a bushel while soybeans were mostly steady.</p>
<p>Hard red winter wheat positions firmed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Despite the rain, Midwest farmers are harvesting corn and just starting on soybeans &quot;and the corn crop looks fairly good,&quot; one dealer said. That may have sparked lower CIF values, the dealer added.</p>
<p>But export activity was sluggish. Taiwanese buyers are expected to hold four tenders for a total of 104,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeansand 88,000 tonnes of corn next week.  </p>
